Package: forestCI
Title: Distance-Dependent and Distance-Independent Competition Indices for Forest Stands
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aaron", "Weiskittel", email = "aaron.weiskittel@maine.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Justin", "Waskiewicz", role = "aut",
           comment = "Original crown geometry and area potentially available algorithms"),
    person("Christian", "Kuehne", role = "aut"))
Description: A generalized implementation of individual-tree competition indices
    for forest stands, covering both the distance-independent family (basal area,
    basal area of larger trees, stand density index, relative density, crown
    competition factor, crown competition factor of larger trees) and the
    distance-dependent family (Hegyi, Spurr, Martin-Ek, Lorimer, Braathe,
    Rouvinen-Kuuluvainen, Canham neighbourhood competition index, local basal
    area, area potentially available from weighted Voronoi tessellation, its
    rasterised form, exposed crown surface area, and open sky view). Indices that
    require stem coordinates are computed when coordinates or distance and azimuth
    are supplied, and the distance-independent set is always available. Crown
    dimensions are obtained from a pluggable crown profile interface with three
    built-in families and softwood or hardwood defaults, so the package generalises
    to species with no local parameterisation. Methods follow Waskiewicz (2011) and
    Kuehne, Weiskittel and Waskiewicz (2019) <doi:10.1016/j.foreco.2018.11.002>.
